<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Database Design and CRUD Operations Table</title>
<!--[if gte mso 9]>
<xml>
<w:WordDocument>
<w:View>Print</w:View>
<w:Zoom>100</w:Zoom>
<w:DoNotOptimizeForBrowser/>
</w:WordDocument>
</xml>
<![endif]-->
<style>
  body {
    font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 11pt;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  h2 {
    color: #1f4e79;
    font-size: 16pt;
    border-bottom: 2pt solid #1f4e79;
    padding-bottom: 4pt;
    margin-bottom: 12pt;
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: 10pt;
    font-size: 10pt;
  }
  th {
    background-color: #1f4e79;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: left;
    padding: 8pt 10pt;
    border: 1pt solid #1f4e79;
  }
  td {
    padding: 7pt 9pt;
    border: 1pt solid #d9d9d9;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  tr:nth-child(even) td {
    background-color: #f2f7fa;
  }
  code {
    font-family: 'Consolas', 'Courier New', monospace;
    color: #c00000;
    background-color: #f2f2f2;
    padding: 1pt 3pt;
    font-size: 9.5pt;
  }
  .entity-header {
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #1f4e79;
    font-size: 10.5pt;
  }
  .op-badge {
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #2e75b6;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h2>Database Entities, CRUD Operations & Implementation Details</h2>
<p><strong>Course:</strong> BACSE344 — Cloud Infrastructure and Architecture | <strong>Student:</strong> ANIKET MOHANTY (25BCE5816)</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 18%;">Entity / Collection</th>
      <th style="width: 12%;">Operation</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">HTTP Method & Endpoint</th>
      <th style="width: 45%;">Implementation Details (Mongoose ODM & Logic)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <!-- AuthUser -->
    <tr>
      <td rowspan="3"><span class="entity-header">AuthUser</span><br><code>authusers</code></td>
      <td><span class="op-badge">CREATE</span></td>
      <td><code>POST /api/auth/register</code></td>
      <td><code>AuthUser.create({ name, email, password })</code><br>• Pre-save hook hashes password via <code>bcrypt.hash(pwd, 12)</code><br>• Issues signed 7-day JWT bearer token</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">READ</span></td>
      <td><code>POST /api/auth/login</code></td>
      <td><code>AuthUser.findOne({ email }).select('+password')</code><br>• Compares via <code>bcrypt.compare(candidate, hash)</code><br>• Returns signed JWT upon successful match</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">READ</span></td>
      <td><code>GET /api/auth/me</code></td>
      <td><code>AuthUser.findById(req.user.id)</code><br>• Validates token via JWT authentication middleware</td>
    </tr>

    <!-- HabitTask -->
    <tr>
      <td rowspan="5"><span class="entity-header">HabitTask</span><br><code>habittasks</code></td>
      <td><span class="op-badge">CREATE</span></td>
      <td><code>POST /api/habits</code></td>
      <td><code>HabitTask.create({ name, type, scheduledDays, color, order, userId: req.user.id })</code><br>• Auto-assigns order from <code>countDocuments</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">READ</span></td>
      <td><code>GET /api/habits</code></td>
      <td><code>HabitTask.find({ userId: req.user.id, isActive: true }).sort({ order: 1 })</code><br>• Optimized by compound index <code>{ userId: 1, order: 1 }</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">UPDATE</span></td>
      <td><code>PUT /api/habits/:id</code></td>
      <td><code>HabitTask.findOneAndUpdate({ _id: id, userId: req.user.id }, req.body, { new: true })</code><br>• Strict multi-tenant user isolation</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">UPDATE</span></td>
      <td><code>PATCH /api/habits/:id/order</code></td>
      <td><code>HabitTask.findOneAndUpdate({ _id: id, userId: req.user.id }, { order: req.body.order }, { new: true })</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">DELETE</span></td>
      <td><code>DELETE /api/habits/:id</code></td>
      <td><code>HabitTask.findOneAndUpdate({ _id: id, userId: req.user.id }, { isActive: false }, { new: true })</code><br>• <strong>Soft Delete:</strong> preserves historical completion analytics</td>
    </tr>

    <!-- DailyCompletion -->
    <tr>
      <td rowspan="4"><span class="entity-header">DailyCompletion</span><br><code>dailycompletions</code></td>
      <td><span class="op-badge">CREATE / UPDATE</span></td>
      <td><code>POST /api/completions/toggle</code></td>
      <td><strong>Atomic Toggle:</strong><br>1. Verifies ownership via <code>HabitTask.findOne({ _id: taskId, userId: req.user.id })</code><br>2. If existing: inverts <code>completed = !completed</code><br>3. If new: creates completion with <code>userId: req.user.id</code><br>• Unique compound index <code>{ taskId: 1, date: 1 }</code> prevents duplicates</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">READ</span></td>
      <td><code>GET /api/completions?month=YYYY-MM</code></td>
      <td><code>DailyCompletion.find({ taskId: { $in: userTaskIds }, date: { $regex: '^YYYY-MM' }, completed: true }).lean()</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">READ</span></td>
      <td><code>GET /api/completions/chart?days=30</code></td>
      <td>Time-series calculation:<br>• For each day: counts completed vs scheduled tasks<br>• Computes daily percentage: <code>(completed / total) * 100</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">READ</span></td>
      <td><code>GET /api/completions/streak/:taskId</code></td>
      <td>While loop checking consecutive days backwards:<br><code>DailyCompletion.findOne({ taskId, date, completed: true })</code></td>
    </tr>

    <!-- Task -->
    <tr>
      <td rowspan="7"><span class="entity-header">Task</span><br><code>tasks</code></td>
      <td><span class="op-badge">CREATE</span></td>
      <td><code>POST /api/tasks</code></td>
      <td><code>Task.create({ title, description, status, priority, category, dueDate, userId: req.user.id })</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">READ</span></td>
      <td><code>GET /api/tasks</code></td>
      <td><code>Task.find({ userId: req.user.id, ...filters }).sort({ [sortBy]: order }).skip(skip).limit(limit).lean()</code><br>• Server-side pagination and regex title search</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">READ</span></td>
      <td><code>GET /api/tasks/:id</code></td>
      <td><code>Task.findOne({ _id: id, userId: req.user.id })</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">UPDATE</span></td>
      <td><code>PUT /api/tasks/:id</code></td>
      <td><code>Task.findOneAndUpdate({ _id: id, userId: req.user.id }, req.body, { new: true, runValidators: true })</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">UPDATE</span></td>
      <td><code>PATCH /api/tasks/:id</code></td>
      <td><code>Task.findOneAndUpdate({ _id: id, userId: req.user.id }, { $set: allowedUpdates }, { new: true })</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">DELETE</span></td>
      <td><code>DELETE /api/tasks/:id</code></td>
      <td><code>Task.findOneAndDelete({ _id: id, userId: req.user.id })</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="op-badge">AGGREGATE</span></td>
      <td><code>GET /api/tasks/stats</code></td>
      <td>Aggregation Pipeline:<br><code>Task.aggregate([{ $match: { userId: req.user.id } }, { $group: { _id: '$status', count: { $sum: 1 } } }])</code><br>• Computes completion rate, overdue tasks, status breakdown</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

</body>
</html>
